    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by two high-efficiency starts facing favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Bryson Stott** (72.46) leads the charge, benefiting from a soft matchup against Roki Sasaki (5.11 xERA) and a prime #5 spot in the order, while **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) provides an elite ceiling against Brandon Young. Both players are seeing significant boosts from their platoon advantage, making them the primary sources of power and run production for LawDog today. **Tyler Freeman** (71.80) and **Matt Chapman** (70.21) also offer strong value against Ryan Feltner; they are prime targets for our strategy, as Feltner\u2019s profile and park environment project well for contact, keeping both in the high-60s to low-70s efficiency tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 45.42 score. While his projection against Griffin was respectable, the combination of a left-on-left platoon disadvantage and the superior efficiency of **Lawrence Butler**\u2014despite **Butler**'s own platoon struggles\u2014forced a conservative approach to protect our games-played caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Will Smith** (41.93), as Jes\u00fas Luzardo represents a legitimate threat to our AVG category; his low score serves as a warning that he is on the bubble of our 40.0 floor. Furthermore, while we are tracking the potential for stolen bases, players like **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo** were relegated to the bench because their raw output projections against tough arms like Ben Brown and Bryan Woo could not justify displacing our higher-scoring core. LawDog remains wary of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for many of our starters, which introduces volatility to these projections should managers shuffle the batting order.",
